@@ -0,0 +1,128 @@
+# Explicit administrative Conductor recovery (LT-127)
+
+This local resolution action is separate from read-only lookup and Bridge's
+local offline operator tooling. It never retries an external mutation or enables
+production writes. Production credentials, real administrative resolution and
+live deployment remain owner-only actions under the release hold.
+
+## Admission and proof
+
+`POST /project/:projectID/accessibility/workqueue/page/:sectionID/operations/:localID/resolve`
+requires an actual verified session, current support/superadmin role in LibreTexts,
+existing project access and the configured project/tenant opt-in. An ordinary
+project editor, including the original write actor, cannot resolve a claim.
+Support privileges are checked again after the scan. The selected operation must
+come from the stored local mapping; browser issuer/jti/action/target/actor fields
+are rejected. The target must still match the original stored binding and one
+unambiguous project section in the approved Johnny sandbox.
+
+The request is strictly validated with the upstream Zod middleware:
+
+```json
+{
+  "expectedVersion": 1,
+  "confirmed": true,
+  "reason": "Operator evidence references and explicit request for a fresh canonical scan"
+}
+```
+
+Use the integer evidence version from the authenticated operation lookup. A
+missing section reports a null version and cannot be resolved. Confirming a
+request is not permission to skip Bridge settlement or invent a terminal outcome.
+
+The server reads authenticated Bridge status using stored issuer/jti, requires
+`outcome: unknown_write`, `reconciliation: resolved` and
+`requires_reconciliation: false`, then performs an actual fresh canonical source
+scan. It checks returned page ID/path, all 50 unique criterion IDs and supported
+statuses, source hash, freshness, error flags and any supplied rendered evidence.
+Automated failures may remain in a valid scan; they remain failures. It does not
+fabricate browser evidence: a source-only scan leaves rendered/human verification
+pending. A second authenticated status lookup must match the same durable
+operation ID and resolution timestamp before local persistence.
+
+The scan is capped at 1 MiB of new evidence. A failed/incomplete/mismatched scan,
+stale version/status, revoked role, unavailable store, changed target/project
+policy or conflicting claim cannot release the pending state. Missing signing
+material does not block this read-and-local-CAS workflow.
+
+## Auditable write-ahead and CAS
+
+1. Append a journaled immutable `resolution` preparation in
+   remedyoperationrecords. It records the verified support actor, reason,
+   original actor/nonce/action/target, durable remote status, expected local
+   version and scan digest/time. It is explicitly `prepared_for_local_cas`;
+   preparation alone never claims success.
+2. One journaled Project CAS checks the exact section/target/version/pending
+   local ID and unchanged project policy. It stores the fresh scan, advances the
+   evidence version, appends a small immutable resolution commit marker and
+   clears only that pending pointer. The applied resolution epoch changes the
+   page fingerprint so old human reviews cannot revive if identical bytes recur.
+3. No required post-CAS append can fail after release. The bounded Project commit
+   marker permanently identifies the winning preparation, even if a later TOC
+   removes the section. Later write intents retain their predecessor resolution
+   reference. A losing concurrent preparation stays auditable but uncommitted.
+
+Project commit markers are private, append-only and explicitly limited to 1,000.
+The final CAS also requires the physical Project document to remain below 12 MiB
+before storing at most 1 MiB of new scan evidence, leaving room below Mongo's
+16 MiB ceiling. Exhaustion refuses further resolution and preserves all history;
+a separately reviewed storage expansion is required, not deletion/compaction.
+Markers are included in administrative operation exports and the matching
+actor/support status response, not ordinary project reads. No new collection,
+transaction or replica-set prerequisite is introduced. Disabled Remedy does not
+initialize optional feature collections.
+
+Failure before a successful CAS leaves the claim held. If a final CAS commits but
+its acknowledgement/reply is lost, do not infer failure or retry automatically:
+read the local pending state and immutable commit marker. The CAS can only commit
+when fresh evidence and the already-durable preparation are present. An unrelated
+claim is never cleared, and a delayed resolver cannot overwrite a winner or a
+later claim.
+
+## Operator order
+
+These are instructions for an approved operator, not steps an agent may run on a
+live system.
+
+1. Follow Bridge `docs/release/lt-159-offline-resolution.md`: drain all writers,
+   establish actual external-request settlement, preserve exact report/evidence,
+   and record the separate offline decision with exclusive ownership and the
+   independent durable fence. Source equality, time, HTTP 4xx or key rotation do
+   not establish settlement. Preserve original unknown outcomes/tombstones.
+2. Restart only after the operator has authorized it and trust/store checks pass.
+   Read the Conductor operation endpoint with the existing approved session.
+   A lookup still mutates nothing; remote resolved status alone does not unlock.
+3. Preserve the current local version and prepare the explicit confirmed request.
+   Submit it only with support/superadmin plus current project policy. For
+   example, using restricted files rather than printing credentials:
+
+```sh
+curl --silent --show-error --fail-with-body \
+  --cookie "$restricted_cookie_jar" \
+  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+  --data-binary "@$restricted_resolution_request" \
+  "$approved_conductor_origin/api/v1/project/$project_id/accessibility/workqueue/page/$section_id/operations/$local_operation_id/resolve"
+```
+
+4. Inspect the returned local resolution ID/version, fresh evidence and read-only
+   operation/commit marker. Remote outcome stays unknown; resolved is an audited
+   settlement decision, not proof of successful editing or WCAG conformance.
+5. On refusal, preserve artifacts and the pending claim. Refresh read-only status;
+   do not perform a global unlock, replay the mutation, remove history, restore
+   an old fence with a database or treat a snapshot restore as settlement.
+
+Back up the full Project (including private commit markers), immutable records,
+user identities and Bridge's ledger/fence/snapshots/trust epoch consistently after
+draining writers. Keep a compatible reader during rollback. Reverting runtime
+code cannot undo an administrative record or make an old pending pointer safe.
+
+## Remaining contract gate
+
+Bridge LT-159 currently resolves active terminal unknown_write operations only.
+A locally pending operation whose remote result is known_success, not_attempted
+or absent cannot obtain resolved through that command. This endpoint deliberately
+keeps those claims held. A known-success result after a lost Conductor reply is
+reproduced in component and actual-service HTTP evidence. The Chief must scope
+any extension to durable receipts/administrative settlement; no generic status
+or source-equality unlock is implemented here. LT-127's broader recovery ticket
+and LT-111 production release remain open for that decision and other gates.
